  "migration_notes": "RFC-042: Orders API v2 changes how an order's money, customer and payment state are represented. The REST payload, the gRPC OrderSummary message and the orders table all change in the same release. Float money caused rounding incidents, so money must be integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency. Consumers should ship tolerant readers that accept v1 and v2 at the same time before Orders deploys v2. REST clients should read total.amount_minor when present, else round(total_price * 100), and gRPC clients should vendor the v2 proto with deprecated fields 2 and 3."
